==Strategy==
The key to success is to send the enemy into a coma by continuously leverage out enough space to lure the Prof. Owlbrowleys and Li'l Buns into the range of your main attackers. They're almost impossible to target whilst behind The Perfect Cyclone, so instantly grab as much of the battlefield as you can as soon as the stage starts and try to keep The Perfect Cyclone still with [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] while [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] (particularly with [[Wave Attack]]) destroy the [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]]/[[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] peons. Bring [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]] to chip the Prof. Owlbrowleys, but try not to spawn him any earlier since he's likely to walk directly into The Perfect Cyclone's effective range and get himself killed. Time Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] on the second Prof. Owlbrowley for some serious chip damage, at which point there will be nothing stopping you from swarming The Perfect Cyclone with [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cats]] and Fishman Cats.

